<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador bank liquidity up 1.7 pct wk to March 14.</title>
<headline>Ecuador bank liquidity up 1.7 pct wk to March 14.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday liquidity in the banking system rose 1.7 percent or 325 million sucres to 18.64 billion sucres in the week to March 14.</p>
<p>At the end of February, bank liquidity stood at 18.37 billion sucres.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the banking sector ended 1996 at 16.99 billion sucres, up 35.8 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
